+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts (Base)
+
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` and its configuration, plus the deploy/verify posture of the
+already-deployed `Payouts` contract. Review only — no code changed.
+
+Reviewed statically: the workspace has no `node_modules`, so the app was not booted.
+Every finding below is read off the source, not inferred from runtime behaviour.
+
+**10 ship-blocking · 13 should-fix**
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. USDC is registered in `deployedContracts.ts` — the next `yarn deploy` erases it
+
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (and `app/payouts/page.tsx:11`)
+
+`deployedContracts.ts` is autogenerated. The hand-added `USDC` entry survives only until
+someone runs `yarn deploy`, at which point the file is rewritten from the deploy artifacts,
+`USDC` disappears, and every USDC read/write on the page dies — `useScaffoldReadContract`
+returns nothing silently, and the type of `deployedContracts[8453].USDC` stops existing so
+the build breaks. This is the single most fragile thing in the app.
+
+**Fix:** move the entry to `externalContracts.ts` and revert `deployedContracts.ts` to its
+generated state (only `Payouts`).
+
+```typescript
+// packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts
+const externalContracts = {
+  8453: {
+    USDC: {
+      address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913",
+      abi: [ /* the ABI currently at deployedContracts.ts:52-133 */ ],
+    },
+  },
+} as const;
+
+export default externalContracts satisfies GenericContractsDeclaration;
+```
+
+Then confirm `yarn next:check-types` passes.
+
+---
+
+### 2. Disconnected users get a sentence instead of a Connect button
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+
+```tsx
+{!isConnected ? (
+  <p className="mt-4">Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p>
+) : (
+```
+
+The page's whole reason to exist is behind a wall of text that tells the user to go find the
+header. The action slot must contain the action.
+
+**Fix:** render the connect button in the action slot.
+
+```tsx
+import { RainbowKitCustomConnectButton } from "~~/components/scaffold-eth";
+
+if (!isConnected) return <RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />;
+```
+
+---
+
+### 3. No wrong-network branch on the primary CTA
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+A wallet on Ethereum mainnet (or Arbitrum, or anything) sees fully enabled **Approve** and
+**Send Payout** buttons. The header's `WrongNetworkDropdown` is passive — nothing in the
+action slot reacts to chain. With the raw wagmi write of finding #4 there is not even the
+scaffold hook's wrong-network guard, so the user signs an approve against whatever USDC-shaped
+address happens to sit at `0x8335…2913` on the chain they are on. Best case the tx reverts;
+worst case they approve a stranger's contract.
+
+**Fix:** the CTA itself becomes the switch button.
+
+```tsx
+const { chain } = useAccount();
+const { targetNetwork } = useTargetNetwork();
+const { switchChain } = useSwitchChain();
+
+if (chain?.id !== targetNetwork.id) {
+  return (
+    <button className="btn btn-primary" onClick={() => switchChain({ chainId: targetNetwork.id })}>
+      Switch to {targetNetwork.name}
+    </button>
+  );
+}
+```
+
+Place it after the connect branch and before the Approve/Action branch, so exactly one
+primary action is ever live: Connect → Switch → Approve → Send.
+
+---
+
+### 4. Writes use raw wagmi `useWriteContract`, not `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21,38-43,51-56`
+
+`writeContractAsync` from bare wagmi resolves the moment the wallet hands back a tx hash —
+**not** when the transaction confirms. So `handlePay` clears the form (lines 57-58) while the
+payout is still in the mempool, and the UI reports success for a transaction that may still
+revert. It also skips everything the scaffold wrapper gives you: pre-flight
+`simulateContractWriteAndNotifyError` (which would surface "transfer amount exceeds allowance"
+*before* the wallet popup), the wrong-network and not-deployed guards, the transactor toasts,
+and `isMining`.
+
+**Fix:** two hooks, one per contract, and let the form clear only after confirmation.
+
+```tsx
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } = useScaffoldWriteContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+});
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({
+  contractName: "Payouts",
+});
+
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+
+Note this depends on #1: `contractName: "USDC"` only type-checks once USDC lives in
+`externalContracts.ts`.
+
+---
+
+### 5. Failed and rejected transactions fail silently
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`
+
+```tsx
+} catch (e) {
+  console.error(e);
+}
+```
+
+Insufficient allowance, insufficient balance, a user rejection, a reverted `pay` — all of them
+produce an unchanged screen and a line in a console the user will never open. On a page that
+moves real money, "nothing happened" is the worst possible failure mode.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+import { getParsedError, notification } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth";
+
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+### 6. Buttons unlock mid-flight because they watch `isPending`, not `isMining`
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21,101-102,108-109`
+
+`isPending` is wagmi's *signature-pending* flag. It goes false as soon as the wallet returns
+the hash, so both buttons re-enable while the payout is still unconfirmed — the user sees a
+live "Send Payout" button, clicks again, and sends a second payout.
+
+**Fix:** use the `isMining` flag from `useScaffoldWriteContract` (#4). It is held across
+`waitForTransactionReceipt` and cleared in the hook's `finally` on both confirmation and
+rejection. If you add an allowance refetch after confirmation, hold the button with local
+state cleared in the same `finally` — never on a `setTimeout`.
+
+---
+
+### 7. Approve and Send Payout are both live, and allowance is never read
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+Two equally-weighted primary buttons side by side with no indication of which one to press,
+and nothing in the page reads `USDC.allowance`. Consequences:
+
+- A user with sufficient allowance is still told to Approve — a pointless transaction and gas.
+- A user with none presses Send Payout first and gets a bare revert (silently, per #5).
+- Approve is for the exact `amount` (line 42), so editing the amount after approving
+  invalidates it, with no feedback anywhere.
+
+**Fix:** read the allowance and let it choose the button.
+
+```tsx
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS.address],
+});
+
+const needsApproval = allowance === undefined || allowance < parseUnits(amount || "0", 6);
+```
+
+Render **Approve** when `needsApproval`, **Send Payout** otherwise — never both. Refetch the
+allowance after the approve confirms.
+
+---
+
+### 8. `fromBlock: 0n` scans all of Base from genesis on every page load
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:32`
+
+`useScaffoldEventHistory` already defaults `fromBlock` to the contract's `deployedOnBlock`,
+which is recorded as `33712450` in `deployedContracts.ts:47`. Passing `0n` explicitly throws
+that away and asks the RPC to walk ~33.7M blocks of Base in paginated `getLogs` calls. On the
+shared Alchemy key (#15) this rate-limits or times out; the payouts feed will read
+"No payouts yet." for users who have made payouts.
+
+**Fix:** drop the `fromBlock` line entirely and let the hook use `deployedOnBlock`.
+
+---
+
+### 9. Hardcoded `bg-black` wrapper bypasses DaisyUI theming
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+
+```tsx
+<div className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white">
+```
+
+The footer ships a working `<SwitchTheme/>` (`components/Footer.tsx:43`) and `globals.css`
+defines full light and dark themes. This wrapper overrides both: light-mode users get a black
+page, the theme toggle does nothing on this route, and DaisyUI components inside it
+(`input input-bordered`, `textarea`) keep rendering their theme-derived light backgrounds
+against black. `min-h-screen` also double-counts the header height and adds a scrollbar.
+
+**Fix:** `<div className="bg-base-200 text-base-content grow">`, and replace the
+`border-gray-700` on line 121 with `border-base-300`.
+
+---
+
+### 10. Recipient is a raw `<input type="text">` cast straight to an address
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84,55`
+
+```tsx
+<input type="text" placeholder="0x... recipient address" ... />
+...
+args: [recipient as `0x${string}`, ...]
+```
+
+No ENS resolution, no checksum validation, no format check — the `as` cast just silences
+TypeScript. `vitalik.eth` is passed to the contract verbatim and the transaction fails with an
+opaque viem error (silently, per #5). A truncated or mistyped hex string that still parses is
+worse: `Payouts.pay` only rejects `address(0)`, so a valid-but-wrong address sends real USDC
+somewhere unrecoverable.
+
+**Fix:** use the scaffold component, which resolves ENS and blocks submission on an invalid
+value.
+
+```tsx
+import { AddressInput } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+
+<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="Recipient address or ENS" />
+```
+
+Also disable the send button while `!isAddress(recipient)`.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 11. DaisyUI `loading` class on a `btn` deletes the label
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101,108`
+
+```tsx
+className={`btn btn-primary ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`}
+```
+
+`loading` on a `btn` replaces the button's contents with a spinner — mid-transaction the user
+sees two unlabelled spinning buttons and cannot tell which action is in flight.
+
+**Fix:** keep the label, add an inline spinner beside it.
+
+```tsx
+<button className="btn btn-primary" disabled={isMining} onClick={handlePay}>
+  {isMining && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm" />}
+  Send Payout
+</button>
+```
+
+---
+
+### 12. Hand-rolled `shorten()` instead of `<Address/>`
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:13,122,124`
+
+The payouts feed prints bare truncated hex. No blockie, no ENS name, no copy button, no
+Basescan link — so a user who wants to confirm a payout landed has to select-and-paste a
+string that is not even fully rendered.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```tsx
+import { Address } from "@scaffold-ui/components";
+
+<Address address={payout.args.from} size="sm" />
+```
+
+Delete the `shorten` helper.
+
+---
+
+### 13. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (whole page)
+
+The page shows the user their own balance but never says which contract is about to move their
+USDC or which contract they are granting an allowance to. For a page whose core ask is
+"approve this contract to spend your money", that is the one address that must be on screen.
+
+**Fix:** under the heading, render
+`<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} chain={targetNetwork} />` with a "Payouts contract" label.
+
+---
+
+### 14. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+Base produces a block every 2 seconds. At a 30-second poll the balance and the payouts feed
+lag by up to half a minute after a confirmed transaction — the app reads as broken or as
+having dropped the payout.
+
+**Fix:** `pollingInterval: 3000`, and explicitly refetch the balance and allowance in the
+write's `onBlockConfirmation` so the post-transaction update is immediate rather than polled.
+
+---
+
+### 15. Production traffic is on Scaffold-ETH's shared Alchemy key
+
+`packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,32-35`
+
+`rpcOverrides` is empty (still the commented-out example), and `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY`
+falls back to `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` — a demo key shared across every SE-2 project on the
+internet. `wagmiConfig.tsx:20` compounds it: when the default key is detected, the Alchemy
+transport is pushed *behind* the bare `http()` fallback, so Base traffic goes first to the
+public `mainnet.base.org` endpoint. Combined with #8 and the watch-mode polling, expect 429s.
+
+**Fix:** provision a real Base RPC and route through the override.
+
+```typescript
+rpcOverrides: {
+  [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL as string,
+},
+```
+
+Add `NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL` to `.env.example`, and **verify it is actually set in the Vercel
+project** — a referenced-but-unset variable silently falls back to the public endpoint.
+`walletConnectProjectId` (line 40) has the same problem: it is SE-2's shared default project
+ID. Register your own.
+
+---
+
+### 16. Scaffold-ETH branding still ships in all five places
+
+- `app/layout.tsx:11-12` — tab title `Scaffold-ETH 2 App`, description `Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2`
+- `utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8` — title template `%s | Scaffold-ETH 2`
+- `public/manifest.json` — `Scaffold-ETH 2 DApp`
+- `components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → scaffold-eth/se-2, "Built with ♥ at BuidlGuidl", and a Support link to the **SE-2 Telegram group**, where your users will go with payout problems
+- `README.md:1` — still the upstream scaffold README
+- `public/favicon.png` / `thumbnail.jpg` — still scaffold defaults; `thumbnail.jpg` is what gets unfurled when someone shares a payout link in Slack
+
+**Fix:** set title to something like `USDC Payouts`, write a real description, replace the
+footer links with your own support channel (keep the BuidlGuidl credit if you want — the
+misrouted Support link is the actual problem), rewrite the README for this app, and swap the
+favicon and thumbnail.
+
+---
+
+### 17. `--radius-field: 9999rem` gives pill-shaped inputs
+
+`packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36,63`
+
+Fully-rounded fields clip the leading characters of a long address and fight the square
+`--radius-box: 0rem` cards around them. The payout form is three stacked fields, so this is the
+page's dominant visual.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in **both** `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks (light at
+line 36, dark at line 63). Do it at theme level, not with per-component `rounded-*`.
+
+---
+
+### 18. Phantom users cannot connect at all
+
+`packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:2-9,20-28`
+
+The wallet list is SE-2's default and has no Phantom. Phantom has a large Base user base and
+does not appear via the injected fallback here, so those users open the modal and find no way in.
+
+**Fix:**
+
+```typescript
+import { phantomWallet } from "@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets";
+
+const wallets = [metaMaskWallet, walletConnectWallet, phantomWallet, ledgerWallet, ...];
+```
+
+While in this file: `appName: "scaffold-eth-2"` (line 49) is what shows in the wallet approval
+prompt — change it to the product name.
+
+---
+
+### 19. Mobile WalletConnect users are stranded on the transaction
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`
+
+On a phone connected over WalletConnect, tapping Approve or Send Payout fires the request and
+leaves the user staring at the dApp — nothing brings the wallet app forward. They have to guess
+that they must switch apps by hand, and most will assume the button is broken.
+
+**Fix:** after initiating the write (never before — navigating away first means the write never
+fires), deep-link to the connected wallet:
+
+```tsx
+const { connector } = useAccount();
+
+const txPromise = writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [...] });
+if (isMobile && connector?.id === "walletConnect") window.location.href = "wc://";
+await txPromise;
+```
+
+Target the wallet the user actually connected with, and skip the redirect inside a wallet's
+in-app browser (where the signing prompt is already in-context).
+
+---
+
+### 20. Confirm `Payouts` is verified on Basescan
+
+`packages/hardhat/` — no `deployments/` directory is present in the repo
+
+The contract is live at `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2` (per
+`deployedContracts.ts:10`) but there are no local deployment artifacts, so verification status
+cannot be confirmed from this workspace. Unverified bytecode on a contract users are asked to
+grant a USDC allowance to reads as something to hide.
+
+**Fix:** check Basescan; if the source is not published, run `yarn verify --network base`.
+Note `hardhat.config.ts:17` also falls back to a shared public `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` — set your
+own before verifying.
+
+---
+
+### 21. Home page is still the scaffold placeholder
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:22,30-45,49-71`
+
+`/` greets real users with "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", instructions to edit `page.tsx`, a
+reference to `YourContract.sol` (which does not exist in this repo — the contract is
+`Payouts.sol`), and cards pointing at Debug Contracts and the Block Explorer.
+
+**Fix:** either make `/` the payouts page, or replace the body with a short product intro and a
+link to `/payouts`. Also drop the **Debug Contracts** entry from `menuLinks`
+(`components/Header.tsx:27-31`) for the production build — it is a developer tool that lets
+anyone call arbitrary contract functions.
+
+---
+
+### 22. Payouts feed renders oldest-first with index keys
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120-121`
+
+The heading says "Latest payouts" but `useScaffoldEventHistory` returns events in ascending
+block order, so the newest payout is at the bottom of an ever-growing unbounded list. `key={i}`
+compounds it: when a new event prepends or the list reorders, React reuses the wrong DOM nodes.
+
+**Fix:** `[...(payouts ?? [])].reverse().slice(0, 20)`, and key on
+`` `${payout.log.transactionHash}-${payout.log.logIndex}` ``.
+
+---
+
+### 23. Balance renders `0` while it is still loading
+
+`packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75`
+
+```tsx
+{usdcBalance !== undefined ? formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6) : "0"}
+```
+
+An undefined balance means "not loaded yet", not "zero". At a 30s polling interval (#14) a user
+with funds is told they have `0 USDC` on every page load and may well close the tab.
+
+**Fix:** take `isLoading` from the hook and render
+`<span className="loading loading-spinner loading-xs" />` while it is true; show `0` only once
+the read has actually resolved.

